aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking For and Giving Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the question<span class=\"italic\"> What should I do?</span> to ask for advice. You can use the modals <span class=\"italic\">should</span> and<span class=\"italic\"> could </span>before the verb to give advice.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "What should I do to lose weight?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You should work it off on your bike. It's good exercise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">You should try to get an autograph from one of the players. </span> <br> <span class=\"italic\">You could try keeping track of the players in this scorebook. </span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Making and Responding to Requests", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you make and respond to requests, remember to be polite!", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Is there any chance you'd be interested in a baseball game?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Yeah, I would enjoy that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Would you mind explaining the game to me?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "No problem.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Making Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Responding to Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would you \u2026 ?</br> I'd like to \u2026</br> Would you mind (if) \u2026 ?</br> Would \u2026  be okay?</br> I was wondering if \u2026 </br>Could you \u2026 ?</br> Do you think you could \u2026 ?</br> Is there any chance you could \u2026 ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sure, I'll \u2026 </br>Sure, I'd be glad to \u2026</br> No, not at all.</br> Certainly.</br> Yes, of course.</br> I'll see what I can do.</br> I don't mind at all.</br> Of course we can \u2026</br> No problem.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lose weight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to decrease your weight ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally wants to lose weight after eating a big lunch. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about diet and exercise.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to work it off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to exercise after a big meal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally and Peter work off the big lunch by bike-riding.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "innovative", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describes something using new and interesting ideas", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The bike share system around the city is really innovative.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take (amount of time)", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the amount of time needed to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It takes 30 minutes to get into the city by train.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "strike", "type